      "prompt": "Discuss organization, not a full rewrite. The single established requirement is concentration prediction from whichever sensors are available. A mask encoder and a masked pooling operation cooperate to meet that one requirement; neither is independently claimed as novel. One combined operation is the candidate advance, with a comparison on independent held-out batches. No second challenge, new task, causal proof or plant deployment has been established. The author has an accurate short abstract and a conclusion summarizing the method and that evaluation; they do not want a future-work paragraph. Should we invent a second challenge to balance the two components, make two independent contribution items, or append diffusion/LLM future work to sound current? Give a concrete alternative organization and the evidence still needed to judge the candidate novelty.",
